My $0.02 on restricting wizard's abilities with weapons:

Right now, however I want to play, it's possible.  If I'm in the mood for 
going down quickly, or slowly, or sacrificing forever at the altar, I can 
do so.  This is part of the fun of Nethack; I almost always play wizards 
but the game changes drastically every time I play it.

If we impose major restrictions and bonuses on all classes, then this dis-
appears.  Where right now, there are infinite directions for play, this way
there would be only about 10 -- one for each player type.  

Am I exaggerating?  Maybe.  But saying 'All wizard's *can't* have trained 
in weapons,' and 'All priests can't eat corpses, because they're unclean,'
and other things like that ... is moving in that direction.  Why limit the 
possibilities for play?

Solutions:

  1) Lots and lots of classes.

  2) Build classes.  A skill-based system for NetHack has been suggested 
     before.

  3) Leave classes the way they are and add new classes with the limitations
     and advantages that have been suggested.  No more work for the coders,
     and theoretically they will even balance with the old for utility.

		-- Ryan S. Borgstrom

